WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:00.800
Hi.

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.580
Howdy.

00:00:01.580 --> 00:00:03.660
So let's say,
hypothetically, there's

00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:07.260
a young man here who is
dating a young woman who

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:08.880
tends to lean very far left.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:18.590
Sorry, before you
go any further,

00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:19.890
is she present right now?

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:20.540
No, she is not.

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:21.706
OK good, so I can be honest.

00:00:21.706 --> 00:00:23.655
Right.

00:00:23.655 --> 00:00:28.010
So do you have any advice
for how this young man might

00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:29.724
go about exposing
her to some new ideas

00:00:29.724 --> 00:00:31.640
without the relationship
crashing and burning?

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:32.120
Oh, you're an optimist.

00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:32.619
OK.

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:41.420
So you, my friend, are
making a very large mistake.

00:00:46.669 --> 00:00:47.710
I'm sure she's wonderful.

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:48.980
I'm sure she's
supremely attractive.

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:50.300
I'm sure all of those things.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:51.980
It depends what the
relationship is for.

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:52.990
Are you in it for marriage?

00:00:52.990 --> 00:00:55.073
Or like, you actually have
to give me like-- well,

00:00:55.073 --> 00:00:56.190
what's the end goal here?

00:00:56.190 --> 00:00:56.980
Yeah, marriage.

00:00:56.980 --> 00:00:58.480
OK, so if you're
in it for marriage,

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:00.550
then the number one thing
you must have in common

00:01:00.550 --> 00:01:02.040
with your spouse is values.

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:03.820
Interests come after values.

00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:05.870
But most people are
interested in lots of things.

00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:07.210
There are lots of interesting
things in the world.

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:09.520
Liking the same movies,
liking the same art,

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:10.720
virtually worthless.

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:13.365
What is important is that you
have the same value system.

00:01:13.365 --> 00:01:14.990
So politics are a
reflection of values.

00:01:14.990 --> 00:01:16.030
Now, there are a
lot of people who

00:01:16.030 --> 00:01:17.870
never connect their
politics with their values.

00:01:17.870 --> 00:01:20.161
So you have to determine
whether she's politically left

00:01:20.161 --> 00:01:21.920
because this represents
some core values,

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:23.770
or just because she's been
told a bunch of slogans,

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:25.090
and now she repeats
all of these slogans.

00:01:25.090 --> 00:01:26.960
So when I first dated
my wife, for example,

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:28.270
my wife thought of
herself as pro-choice.

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:30.070
And then the more that
we discussed the issue,

00:01:30.070 --> 00:01:32.440
it became very clear to her
that she was actually pro-life,

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:34.270
and hadn't really considered
the issue in a serious way.

00:01:34.270 --> 00:01:36.110
It was just, she was
told on college campus

00:01:36.110 --> 00:01:37.859
that it was a good
thing to be pro-choice.

00:01:37.859 --> 00:01:39.400
And so she said
she was pro-choice.

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:42.010
And the same thing was true
of gun rights, for example.

00:01:42.010 --> 00:01:43.510
She didn't know
anything about guns.

00:01:43.510 --> 00:01:45.040
She'd been told guns were bad.

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:46.930
And then, when I explained
gun rights to her,

00:01:46.930 --> 00:01:48.680
and when it turned out
that her father was

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:52.150
a member of the military,
then she shifted a little bit.

00:01:52.150 --> 00:01:53.930
Politics is the
tip of the iceberg.

00:01:53.930 --> 00:01:57.250
The question is whether
your girlfriend's politics--

00:01:57.250 --> 00:02:01.690
or this unnamed person's
girlfriend's politics--

00:02:01.690 --> 00:02:04.180
are a floating bit of flotsam
on the top of the ocean,

00:02:04.180 --> 00:02:06.970
or whether there's actually
a structural underpinning

00:02:06.970 --> 00:02:07.990
for what she's thinking.

00:02:07.990 --> 00:02:09.370
So you first have
to determine that.

00:02:09.370 --> 00:02:11.200
If there is a structural
underpinning, and if she really

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:13.010
believes this stuff
on a strong level,

00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:14.050
you're really going
to have to think about

00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:16.050
whether this is something
you want to go through

00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:17.140
for the next 80 years.

00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:19.840
Because when it comes
time to raise your kids--

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:20.710
forget about you.

00:02:20.710 --> 00:02:23.092
OK, in my view, marriage
is-- marriage, not

00:02:23.092 --> 00:02:25.300
relationships-- marriage is
about bearing and rearing

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:26.150
children.

00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:27.430
Ideally.

00:02:27.430 --> 00:02:29.040
My wife and I have two children.

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:30.610
That is the end
goal of marriage.

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:32.000
That is the telos of marriage.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:34.540
Marriage was created so
that we could bear and raise

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:35.182
our children.

00:02:35.182 --> 00:02:36.640
And that means that
we have to have

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:39.099
very similar perspectives on
how we want to raise our kids.

00:02:39.099 --> 00:02:41.473
Now, if you want to raise your
kid with traditional ideas

00:02:41.473 --> 00:02:43.122
of virtue and
decency, and she wants

00:02:43.122 --> 00:02:44.830
to raise your kids
with traditional ideas

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:47.260
of multiculturalism,
for example,

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:49.970
and all cultures and all
opinions being equal,

00:02:49.970 --> 00:02:51.370
all behavior being
equal, this is

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:53.020
going to be a real
conflict when it comes time

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:53.960
to parent your kids.

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:56.500
So you have to ask
yourself two questions.

00:02:56.500 --> 00:02:58.330
One, is she movable?

00:02:58.330 --> 00:03:02.230
And two, if she's not movable,
what is your end goal, here?

00:03:02.230 --> 00:03:04.650
Because you know, there's
lots of fun to be had in life.

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:06.150
But when it comes
time for marriage,

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:08.274
marriage is-- as all the
married people in the room

00:03:08.274 --> 00:03:10.180
know-- marriage is
not the time for fun.

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:15.122
You know, when it comes
time for marriage--

00:03:15.122 --> 00:03:15.830
not totally true.

00:03:15.830 --> 00:03:17.663
I love my wife and we
have a great marriage.

00:03:17.663 --> 00:03:20.920
But-- see, I know
she's watching.

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:24.010
But when it comes
time for marriage,

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:26.851
it is deeply important that
you put values before all

00:03:26.851 --> 00:03:28.100
of the other ancillary things.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:29.230
If you have values in
common, your marriage

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:30.010
can outlast anything.

00:03:30.010 --> 00:03:31.480
If you don't have
values in common,

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:34.200
then the first break,
and the the thing's over.

